# Global Standards

Any task MUST begin by initializing the protocol in `agent-pipeline.mdc` (Discovery → Simulation → TDD Execution → Verification → Brain Sync → Confidence). Domain standards live in their own rules; the pipeline enforces them — never bypass it.

## 0.1 Conditional Rule Routing (CRITICAL)

Do NOT assume Cursor auto-attaches glob-scoped rules: `alwaysApply: false` rules attach inconsistently, so before planning or editing in a task area, **explicitly read the matching rules**:

- **React / component / hook / page / HOC work** → `react-patterns.mdc`, `engineering-standards.mdc`, `performance.mdc`
- **New behavioral component or changed behavior** → also `test-driven-development.mdc` before implementation
- **Tests / specs / fixtures / mocks** → `test-driven-development.mdc`
- **API client / TanStack Query / data-fetching / payload contracts** → `api.mdc`, `resilience.mdc`, `engineering-standards.mdc`
- **Zustand stores / selectors / server-state** → `state-management.mdc`, `resilience.mdc`, `engineering-standards.mdc`
- **Router / route organization / pages** → `routing.mdc`
- **Async / error handling / debugging** → `resilience.mdc`
- **Styling / render-perf / memo / list keys** → `performance.mdc` + `react-patterns.mdc`
- **Constants / magic strings / config values** → `constants.mdc`, `engineering-standards.mdc`
- **UI / Tailwind v4 / i18n resources / accessibility / base-layer states** → `project-config.mdc`
- **PWA / service worker / `vite.config.ts` / manifest / `index.html` meta / MSW** → `project-config.mdc` §PWA + **mandatory** `.cursor/brain/PWA.md` + `.cursor/brain/SKELETONS.md` (load-bearing, destructive-to-change config)

Always-on rules (`agent-pipeline.mdc`, `global.mdc`, `workflow.mdc`) attach automatically — they need not appear in the Rule Receipt (`agent-pipeline.mdc` Step 1).

## Standards

- **Language**: English only — source, identifiers, comments, JSDoc, tests and Git messages (`type(scope): subject`, `workflow.mdc`). Brain/docs under `.cursor/brain/` may be English for template consistency; no Russian in production code or commits.
- **Authority**: `AGENTS.md` § Start here — code is ground truth, `AGENTS.md` the canonical guide, `.cursor/brain/` the depth layer; sync drift in the same session.
- **Tools**: `sequential-thinking` (if available) for logic, `context7` for docs lookups.
- **Quality**: strict TypeScript; prefer existing libs over custom logic; minimalist code; no magic strings (constants or i18n keys); descriptive names; explain complex logic with single-line `//` only.
- **Hygiene**: AI metadata and agent-only specs stay in `.cursor/`; normal project docs (`README.md`, deployment checklists) may live in the root when they are part of the template contract.
